From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:21:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: BOB1 next to
 stock's 3.296 V

BOB1 supplies the WCD9395's microphone-bias regulator. The codec driver
enables it without a voltage request, so Linux kept whatever the boot
chain had voted (3.032 V). Stock's codec node asks for 3.296 V
(qcom,cdc-vdd-mic-bias-voltage), stock's regulator node starts at that
voltage (qcom,init-voltage), and the vendor kernel shows 3296 mV at run
time.

The regulator's table moves in 32 mV steps from 3.0 V, so 3.296 V itself
cannot be asked for: raise the lower bound to 3.288 V, the nearest step
that does not exceed stock's vote. The upper bound is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 073eaee1fd56..f2c3acb8be5d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -520,9 +520,13 @@ regulators-0 {
 		vdd-l17-supply = <&vreg_bob2>;
 		vdd-l18-supply = <&vreg_s7f_1p2>;
 
+		/*
+		 * stock votes 3.296 V for the codec's microphone-bias supply; 3.288 V is the 32 mV step of this
+		 * regulator's table nearest to it without exceeding it
+		 */
 		vreg_bob1: bob1 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_bob1";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <3008000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3288000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <4000000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
